# Fictional portfolio forward exercise

All repositories, jobs, files and observations in this exercise are fictional.

Use the current Right Shape skill in Audit mode on `sources.json`. Produce one report in this directory named `response.md`; do not change any source record. The owner wants a useful public catalog and a reversible consolidation path. They explicitly want to retain the BASIC learning experiment and leave the upstream fork public. Those decisions are settled. Implementation, publication and retirement are outside this exercise.

Inspect the actual supplied bodies rather than treating repository names as capability names. Give exact existing paths and proposed destinations/interfaces. Separate current evidence from audience/pain hypotheses and asset value. Reconcile all source repositories and embedded methods, explain install blockers, and include the smallest next validation and rollback. Use the canonical rubric; do not invent usefulness ratings if their rubric is unavailable. Stop with the report and only unresolved decisions that change the next action.


